# Agent Workflow: Chain Execution

Purpose:
  Step-by-step workflow for an AI agent using the chain graph.

Agent Entry:
  Read .sdd/PROJECT.sdd
  Read .sdd/chains/graph.sdd
  Read .sdd/chains/selector.sdd

Workflow:
  Step 1: Receive input
    - Human prompt or trigger
    - Determine chain type: selector.sdd -> node_id

  Step 2: Enter graph
    - Start at D0
    - Record token start: tokens_in

  Step 3: Branch to arm
    - D0 -> selected arm (P1/D1/S1/C1/R1/DEP1)
    - Load arm definition
    - Load chain rules
    - Execute arm stages

  Step 4: Arm execution
    - For each stage in arm:
      - Load skills
      - Execute logic
      - Validate output
      - Record token delta
    - If human gate: wait for approval

  Step 5: Return to D0
    - Arm completes
    - Return to D0
    - Record tokens_out
    - Record tokens_delta

  Step 6: Next arm or complete
    - If more arms needed: go to Step 3
    - If complete: finish

Token Rules:
  - Every stage MUST record tokens_in, tokens_out, tokens_delta
  - Total tokens MUST NOT exceed budget
  - If exceeded: use shorter skills, skip optional stages

Human Gates:
  - P1: after docs generated
  - D1: after docs reviewed
  - S1: after .sdd/project/ created
  - C1: after code generated
  - R1: after review
  - DEP1: before production deploy

Error Handling:
  - Retry max 3 times
  - If still failing: escalate to human
   - Record error in token file

State: +
